.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers a callback function that is invoked each time the debugger
stops at a breakpoint or after a step/next/finish operation.
The callback receives a \f[CR]bc_break_hit_event_t\f[R] describing the
stopped command.
.PP
Only one break\-hit callback may be registered at a time.
Calling this function again replaces the previous callback and userdata.
Pass NULL as \f[CR]cb\f[R] to unregister the callback entirely.
.PP
The callback is invoked from within \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] when a
break\-hit event message is received from \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R] (channel
4).
The \f[CR]event\f[R] pointer is valid only for the duration of the
callback invocation; the caller must copy any data it needs to retain.
.PP
