.PP
\f[B]Common callback actions:\f[R]
.PP
Within the callback, the following debug operations are typically
performed:
.IP "1." 3
Inspect the current state with \f[CR]bc_debug_inspect_ast()\f[R] or
\f[CR]bc_debug_status()\f[R].
.IP "2." 3
Query shell variables with \f[CR]bc_state_get()\f[R].
.IP "3." 3
Choose a resumption strategy:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]bc_debug_continue()\f[R] \(em run to next breakpoint
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]bc_debug_step()\f[R] \(em step into
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]bc_debug_next()\f[R] \(em step over
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]bc_debug_finish()\f[R] \(em run until block returns
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]bc_debug_skip()\f[R] \(em skip without executing
.RE
.PP
If no resumption command is issued from the callback, execution remains
paused.
The next \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] call will not receive further events until
a resumption command is sent.
